 ### Coupled Architecture
-Uses a shared network or shared features for geometry and color. This structure boosts depth estimation and Signed Distance Function (SDF) convergence for MLP, Dense, and Sparse representations, reducing Depth L1 loss by approximately 25% in MLP models during initialization [S1]. However, it may compromise color rendering accuracy in Dense (0.91dB drop) and Sparse (1.97dB drop) methods [S1].
+Uses a shared network or shared features for geometry and color [S1]. This structure boosts depth estimation and Signed Distance Function (SDF) convergence for MLP, Dense, and Sparse representations, reducing Depth L1 loss by approximately 25% in MLP models during initialization [S1]. However, it compromises color rendering accuracy in Dense (0.91dB drop) and Sparse (1.97dB drop) methods [S1].
 
 ### Decoupled Architecture
-Uses separate networks for geometry and appearance. This structure benefits decomposition methods (such as Tri-plane and Factorization), showing enhanced geometric accuracy (0.08cm and 0.12cm reduction in Depth L1 loss) and appearance fidelity compared to coupled structures [S1].
